Well, this will be a good place to camp for tonight.

00:26:23.840 --> 00:26:25.800
There's still two hours of daylight left.

00:26:25.800 --> 00:26:29.150
I know, Mr. Darian, but the, uh...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.090
The animals are all worn out.

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:33.650
Poor beasts.

00:26:33.650 --> 00:26:35.810
So are all of us.

00:26:35.810 --> 00:26:38.040
We've traveled a long way.

00:26:38.040 --> 00:26:40.240
But our fear has been that the land will be taken

00:26:40.240 --> 00:26:42.560
before we get there.

00:26:42.560 --> 00:26:44.460
Forgive us, Adam, if we seem impatient,

00:26:44.460 --> 00:26:49.720
but we're so anxious to reach our new home.

00:26:49.720 --> 00:26:52.940
Well, what about it, Hoss, do you think that old trail

00:26:52.940 --> 00:26:56.320
across the plateau might still be good?

00:26:56.320 --> 00:26:59.420
Well, I'm with them and they've been traveling along, Dan.

00:26:59.420 --> 00:27:00.000
Get them wagons.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:08.240
crosshair or not. Don't you think it's still worth a look-see? Yeah. Water your animals,

00:27:08.240 --> 00:27:15.080
but leave them hitched up. We'll see if we can't get you a little further along. Thank you, Adam.

00:27:43.020 --> 00:27:52.670
Hey, wait a minute.

00:27:52.670 --> 00:27:55.350
Fresh tracks, Adam, not over an hour old.

00:27:55.350 --> 00:27:59.130
How many do you figure?

00:27:59.130 --> 00:28:00.000
Well, looks like at least one.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:06.490
Well, whoever they are, they could see the wagons all day.

00:28:06.490 --> 00:28:08.330
I never knew a man yet didn't come into a wagon train

00:28:08.330 --> 00:28:10.300
and get some good home cooking.

00:28:10.300 --> 00:28:11.680
Yeah, me neither.

00:28:11.680 --> 00:28:14.060
Unless they had a reason for not wanting to be seen.

00:28:14.060 --> 00:28:16.120
Well, those wagons and the stock alone,

00:28:16.120 --> 00:28:17.770
that train's good pickings.

00:28:17.770 --> 00:28:19.370
Yeah, if they're planning to do anything about it,

00:28:19.370 --> 00:28:21.160
it'll probably be tonight.

00:28:36.720 --> 00:28:40.200
- Is something amiss? - There's something I have to tell you.

00:28:40.200 --> 00:28:43.500
- What is it, my friend? - A few people have any guns on this train.

00:28:43.500 --> 00:28:47.690
That you use for hunting or anything else, get 'em out.

00:28:47.690 --> 00:28:53.650
What I'm trying to say is that we found the tracks of four horses up there.

00:28:53.650 --> 00:28:58.580
We have reason to believe that these four men have been watching and following this train all day long.

00:29:00.670 --> 00:29:03.670
Do you want them to come in and take everything you own without fighting for it?

00:29:03.670 --> 00:29:06.230
Surely you must have some guns of some kind.

00:29:06.230 --> 00:29:08.410
We have no guns, Adam.

00:29:08.410 --> 00:29:12.060
And we can do no violence on our fellow man.

00:29:12.060 --> 00:29:15.600
Well, they can do violence on their fellow man. And they will.

00:29:15.600 --> 00:29:19.860
Still, it would not be right for us, Matthew.

00:29:19.860 --> 00:29:25.590
Can't you do something?

00:29:25.590 --> 00:29:30.000
He's only thinking of us fighting.

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:36.990
Regina! Hast thou forgotten what we all live by?

00:29:36.990 --> 00:29:43.610
We shall pray that this test comes not to us,

00:29:43.610 --> 00:29:47.920
and that once more we shall be delivered.

00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:52.400
Mr. Darren, don't you reckon you could pray just as well

00:29:52.400 --> 00:29:55.400
if the wagons were circled up and they thought you were going to put up a fight?

00:29:55.400 --> 00:29:58.200
I can't see how that violates nothing.

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:14.990
- Whatever thee thinks best, Mr. Cartwright. - Yes, sir.

00:30:14.990 --> 00:30:28.710
- Adam, he would use this on a man? - I have to.

00:30:55.150 --> 00:31:00.000
will stay beside the atom. If thou canst believe with us, then I will try to believe

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:27.750
We may not have to use them.

00:31:30.440 --> 00:31:33.400
I see the wagons circled, it might make him skittish.

00:31:33.400 --> 00:31:36.090
They don't seem very skittish to me.

00:31:36.090 --> 00:31:38.650
Seems like they got lots of confidence.

00:31:38.650 --> 00:31:55.190
That is thy friend.

00:32:10.590 --> 00:32:12.290
He's made some friends.

00:32:40.270 --> 00:32:43.570
- Easy pickin', son. - Easiest.

00:32:43.880 --> 00:32:47.120
Yeah, they were just gonna invite you right in, as soon as you got here.

00:32:49.790 --> 00:32:50.750
You won't need that.

00:32:51.470 --> 00:32:55.560
That's what you told me, Sam. But you told me a lot of things.

00:32:56.350 --> 00:32:59.830
Now, I'm gonna tell you somethin'. I wanna pick that up.

00:33:00.190 --> 00:33:23.140
easy or any way i can get it and i want to pick it up now wait here too quiet let's wake him up

00:33:58.670 --> 00:33:59.800
to do this.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:05.190
my friend. Get out of my--

00:35:09.500 --> 00:35:15.790
Earth to earth, ashes to ashes, dust to dust.

00:35:15.790 --> 00:35:20.200
Ensure and certain hope of resurrection into eternal life.

00:35:20.200 --> 00:35:30.000
We will move on at once, my friends. Prepare.

00:35:50.830 --> 00:35:55.470
- You will leave me too, Adam? - I have to.

00:35:55.470 --> 00:36:00.000
I brought Sam board among you, and he did all this to you.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:01.000
are not thine.

00:36:01.560 --> 00:36:02.380
In a way they are.

00:36:03.960 --> 00:36:04.660
It's my job

00:36:04.660 --> 00:36:05.780
to get that money back.

00:36:11.430 --> 00:36:15.780
I better go with him.

00:37:03.100 --> 00:37:04.710
Probably head south.

00:37:04.710 --> 00:37:06.760
Bord needs a new town.

00:37:06.760 --> 00:37:15.290
Yep. Man like that's always needing a new town, I reckon.

00:37:15.290 --> 00:37:21.320
Real pretty, isn't it?

00:37:31.440 --> 00:37:34.960
Yeah, it really looks good.

00:37:34.960 --> 00:37:38.160
I'm gonna enjoy it. All of it.

00:37:38.160 --> 00:37:46.330
Why, we're partners, Shed.

00:37:46.330 --> 00:37:48.560
Are we?

00:37:48.560 --> 00:37:50.560
No, I don't figure it that way, Sam.

00:37:52.350 --> 00:37:54.350
As I remembered, you owed me and the boys.

00:37:54.350 --> 00:37:56.370
Since they ain't here to collect,

00:37:56.370 --> 00:37:58.770
I just figured to take all our shares.

00:38:00.480 --> 00:38:01.710
Don't you trust me?

00:38:01.710 --> 00:38:04.490
No, I don't, Sam.

00:38:04.490 --> 00:38:11.490
Now, you just throw the money over here.

00:38:11.490 --> 00:38:16.520
Right down there.

00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:21.560
Oh, and I'll, uh, a heavy gun.

00:38:21.560 --> 00:38:22.850
Real easy.

00:38:22.850 --> 00:38:29.640
But first, right down there, too.

00:38:43.950 --> 00:38:47.540
Could have had half, you never did have any brains.

00:39:01.210 --> 00:39:19.940
Could be a trap, I guess.

00:39:21.450 --> 00:39:23.230
The board's gone all the way now, Adam.

00:39:23.230 --> 00:39:23.650
He's a killer.

00:39:27.430 --> 00:39:28.730
Ain't but one of them left now.

00:39:30.220 --> 00:39:33.650
And that's where the money is.

00:40:34.730 --> 00:40:38.390
- Where's the man who belongs to that horse? - I don't know. He left him here.

00:40:38.540 --> 00:40:41.760
He took another and gave me a $20 gold piece.

00:40:41.920 --> 00:40:43.740
Not more than two hours ago.

00:40:43.850 --> 00:40:47.120
- Which way did he go? - West toward Toe Bridge Creek.

00:40:47.190 --> 00:40:53.750
- We'd like some fresh horses. - We ain't in a hurry, huh?

00:41:19.420 --> 00:41:21.400
the trail again.

00:41:21.400 --> 00:41:24.920
Adam, he ain't doin' a bloomin' thing but leadin' us on one big merry chase round and

00:41:24.920 --> 00:41:26.720
round a circle on these bloomin' rocks.

00:41:26.720 --> 00:41:30.000
Well, sooner or later, he's gotta go to water.

00:41:33.260 --> 00:41:35.530
Or even I don't know you now

00:41:37.600 --> 00:42:00.000
Have to find a town now. Yeah, which one's nearest? Slatersville. Hey, that's where?

00:42:00.350 --> 00:42:01.120
That's right.

00:42:45.610 --> 00:42:46.530
Howdy.

00:42:46.530 --> 00:42:47.580
Howdy.

00:42:47.580 --> 00:42:51.120
What'd I do for you?

00:42:51.120 --> 00:42:56.110
This fit any animal you got in here today?

00:42:56.110 --> 00:42:57.110
Might and I rode to death.

00:42:57.110 --> 00:42:58.510
Going to get him another horse tonight.

00:42:58.510 --> 00:43:00.000
You got any idea where the horse is?

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:03.960
man is? I wouldn't be surprised he's over saluting there cooling his dampers.

00:43:03.960 --> 00:43:07.490
Pretty hot out today. Thanks.

00:43:54.990 --> 00:43:57.360
Miss Regina! Miss Regina!

00:44:01.310 --> 00:44:03.790
Oh, horse. Where is he? Where's Adam? Is he?

00:44:03.910 --> 00:44:04.670
He's all right, ma'am.

00:44:05.090 --> 00:44:07.180
Thank God. But where?

00:44:07.600 --> 00:44:10.910
Ma'am, the board's down here, and Adam's gone after him.

00:44:11.110 --> 00:44:11.610
Oh, no.

00:44:12.290 --> 00:44:15.750
Ma'am, I know how you feel, and I know how Adam feels.

00:44:16.360 --> 00:44:17.880
There ain't nothing nobody can do to stop him.

00:44:18.360 --> 00:44:19.760
The only thing we can do is try to help him.

00:44:20.200 --> 00:44:21.780
Horse, I've got to find him.

00:44:22.310 --> 00:44:26.070
Adam!

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.640
- Adam, I beg thee, thou must not do this thing.

00:44:33.640 --> 00:44:35.480
- What about your father, these people?

00:44:35.480 --> 00:44:38.010
- For whatever the reason, it would be violence.

00:44:38.010 --> 00:44:39.570
Adam, I see vengeance in thine eyes.

00:44:39.570 --> 00:44:41.910
I saw it when thee rode off.

00:44:41.910 --> 00:44:43.210
- Gotta get that money back.

00:44:43.210 --> 00:44:44.730
- If thee get it this way with a gun,

00:44:44.730 --> 00:44:46.820
then it is not worth having.

00:44:46.820 --> 00:44:49.000
They will find him and he will be killed,

00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:50.480
or thee will be killed.

00:44:50.480 --> 00:44:52.440
- I'm sorry.

00:44:52.440 --> 00:44:53.720
- Adam, if thee do this thing,

00:44:53.720 --> 00:44:55.670
it will be between us all our lives.

00:45:00.440 --> 00:45:01.660
It has to be done, Regina.

00:45:02.530 --> 00:45:04.490
You'll get over it.

00:45:05.210 --> 00:45:05.610
Will I?

00:45:07.340 --> 00:45:08.250
Look at me, Adam.

00:45:08.310 --> 00:45:09.170
I am no child.

00:45:10.340 --> 00:45:13.060
I've waited a long time to find the kind of a man I could love.

00:45:13.580 --> 00:45:14.320
Listen to her, Adam.

00:45:15.070 --> 00:45:16.310
You know I don't have any choice.

00:45:16.770 --> 00:45:18.190
I'm responsible for Sam Board.

00:45:18.730 --> 00:45:20.290
They are not responsible to him.

00:45:20.810 --> 00:45:22.650
They are responsible to nobody but thyself.

00:45:23.680 --> 00:45:25.560
Adam, I beg thee, put away thy gun.

00:45:28.050 --> 00:45:30.000
Adam, no!

00:45:30.410 --> 00:45:31.420
No!

00:45:31.840 --> 00:45:33.540
But we befriended thee!

00:45:33.640 --> 00:45:35.250
Get out of the way, old man.

00:45:37.220 --> 00:45:39.120
I've run all I'm gonna run.

00:45:39.440 --> 00:45:41.270
- Boss, get her out of here! - Adam!

00:45:41.390 --> 00:45:43.030
No! No!

00:46:04.350 --> 00:46:05.350
I had to do it.

00:46:05.350 --> 00:46:27.200
Do you have to ride now?

00:46:27.200 --> 00:46:28.680
Yes.

00:46:30.190 --> 00:46:31.370
that he would come and visit us?

00:46:32.810 --> 00:46:35.460
No, I couldn't do that,

00:46:36.480 --> 00:46:39.240
knowing what it would do to you and them.

00:46:40.860 --> 00:46:43.050
And to thee, Adam?

00:46:43.720 --> 00:46:45.800
And me, yes.

00:46:46.930 --> 00:46:53.850
He was my father, Adam, their leader.

00:46:54.780 --> 00:47:00.000
I would be breaking faith with him and them and myself.

00:47:00.160 --> 00:47:01.000
- What if I?

00:47:01.000 --> 00:47:13.250
- Neither one of us had a choice, did we?

00:47:13.250 --> 00:47:14.080
- The atom.

00:47:31.120 --> 00:47:41.430
- No, madam.
